u_{\mu}$ decay mode, which is an important process for determining the $|V_{cb}|$ coefficient using data from the LHCb. A comprehensive analysis of previous studies and new calculations using SYNUA and HOPES, with both approaches taking into account weak annihilation contributions and 5-body intermediate processes, is presented. The results show that the form factors and shape functions for this decay mode have a similar dependence on the momentum of the $D_s^{*-}$ meson. The contributions from both strong and electromagnetic interactions to hadronization are also calculated. The impact of these calculations on measuring the $|V_{cb}|$ coefficient using this decay mode is discussed. The COUETAROUS-QM and BONDE-PETRUSIE-QM approaches are compared to determine the most accurate method for calculating the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate. The findings suggest that both approaches yield comparable outcomes, with the COUETAROUS-QM method slightly preferred due to its higher precision. The dominant source of uncertainty in this calculation comes from the hadronization process, primarily resulting from the number of degrees of freedom during the hadronization of quarks and mesons. The contribution from the hadronization process to the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
